assistant: Subject: Parse epoch-millisecond created_at in get_order

Vendor API version 2026-10-01 sends `created_at` as a number of milliseconds since 1970 (1792142857943, which is 2026-10-16T09:27Z). The published spec still describes it as an ISO-8601 string. `get_order` turned the value into text and passed it to `Date.parse`, which can't read a plain number. Its `|| 0` fallback then quietly changed the failure into 1970-01-01. The fix is in `src/tools/get_order.ts`: when `created_at` is a number, the handler now builds the date from those milliseconds directly. ISO strings go through the same parsing as before, so the v1 output is unchanged. Typecheck, lint and all tests pass, though I didn't add a test for the number-format response. The `|| 0` fallback is still there, so any other unreadable value would still show up as 1970-01-01.

